# Review ownership.
#
# Every file requires review from the listed owner before it can be merged.
# This is what makes the protected-branch rule "Require review from Code
# Owners" actually require a human, rather than just requiring green checks.
#
# IMPORTANT — this file does nothing until the handle below is a real account.
# GitHub does not error on an unresolvable owner; it simply stops requiring
# anyone's review, silently. Replace the placeholder before relying on it.
#
# --- Adapting this file -----------------------------------------------------
# Replace @your-github-handle with a real account on every line.

# Blanket rule: everything needs the owner.
*                       @your-github-handle

# Extra-sensitive paths get an explicit line as well. These are redundant with
# the rule above while there is a single owner, but they are:
#   - self-documenting (the file states what is considered sensitive)
#   - load-bearing the moment a second reviewer is added and the blanket rule
#     is narrowed, because these lines keep the sensitive paths with the owner
/.github/               @your-github-handle
/gitlab-ci/             @your-github-handle
/github-actions/        @your-github-handle
/sonar-project.properties @your-github-handle

# The deployment definition itself. A change here changes what runs in
# production, so it should never be the thing a reviewer skims past.
/gitlab-ci/docker-compose.yml  @your-github-handle
